# Week 2 – Multiple LLM Providers

## Description
This project demonstrates how to integrate multiple LLM providers using Python. Users can choose between Google Gemini (cloud-based) and Ollama (locally running LLM) to generate responses.

## Technologies Used
- Python
- Google Gemini API
- Ollama (Llama 3.2)
- Requests
- python-dotenv

## Features
- Supports both Gemini and Ollama.
- Allows users to select an LLM provider.
- Uses a common interface for different providers.
- Accepts user prompts and generates responses.
- Supports local and cloud-based LLM execution.

## Setup and Execution
1. Install the required libraries:
   ```bash
   pip install google-genai requests python-dotenv
